# Electron Security

- Keep `webSecurity`, context isolation, and sandboxing enabled.
- Expose one narrow typed preload method per operation; never expose raw
  `ipcRenderer`, Node modules, or arbitrary channel names.
- Validate sender frame/window and every payload in the main process.
- Canonicalize paths, reject traversal/symlink escapes, allowlist extensions,
  and restrict access to the user-selected StreamingAssets root.
- Limit payload sizes and use atomic writes for authoritative JSON.
- Restrict navigation/window creation and allow only trusted external URL
  schemes and hosts.
- Add negative tests for untrusted senders, malformed payloads, traversal,
  symlink escape, oversized data, and interrupted writes.
